course: dictionary
lesson: 15712
title: Describing messy hair
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in just one word. Tousled is one of them. It means untidy and messy, especially of hair. «Mia came down to breakfast with tousled hair and a big yawn.» The words tousled hair and big yawn tell you she has only just got out of bed.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The wind tousled the boy's hair as he ran across the beach.» The wind is blowing, so the hair is messy. You can picture the scene without needing a long description.
explain: Tousled is an adjective, a describing word, so it tells you about a noun such as hair, a face or a person. It comes from the verb tousle, which means to make hair messy. Grown-ups sometimes tousle a child's hair as a kind, playful gesture.
fact: Tousled means untidy and messy, especially of hair.
fact: Tousled hair often looks as if you have just woken up.
fact: Tousle is the verb, and tousled is the describing word: he tousled my hair, and my hair was tousled.
fact: The wind can tousle your hair when you are outside on a windy day.
fact: Tousled is the opposite of neat, which means tidy and in order.
exercise: «Mia came down to breakfast with tousled hair and a big yawn.» What does tousled mean? | Wet from the bath | *Untidy and messy | Long and curly | Neatly brushed and shiny
exercise: «The wind tousled the boy's hair as he ran across the beach.» Find and copy the word that tells you what the wind did to his hair. | ran | beach | across | *tousled
exercise: Which person has tousled hair? | A man with his hair cut very short and tidy | A girl with her hair in a neat plait | *A boy who has just woken up, with hair sticking out in all directions | A woman with a smooth, shiny bob
test: Why might a grown-up tousle a child's hair? | To make them cry | *As a kind, playful gesture | To give the child a haircut | To tell them to tidy their room
test: Which word means the opposite of tousled? | Messy | *Neat | Wild | Tangled
exam: Which sentence describes someone's hair as tousled? | She tousled the sky with a blue ribbon. | The shop sold tousled shoes. | The lesson was tousled into three parts. | *He ran in from the storm, and his hair was tousled and messy.
